  "foaf:name": "Ocean Literacy Programme for coastal communities in Ecuador",
  "sdo:name": "Ocean Literacy Programme for coastal communities in Ecuador",
  "sdo:description": "Our Ocean Literacy Program for Coastal communities is a pilot model of a sustainable community to achieve community development based on ocean education, management and sustainable use of resources. It has several projects that, in a holistic way, seek to co-construct oceanic knowledge and relationships through educational, experiential, and experimental processes with the different groups and blue economy sectors with whom we work through our ESRA methodology.  In 8 years, we have benefited more than 19k participants in 38 communities, collecting more than 12 tons of garbage. In every project we seek to: 1) Encourage reflection and critical thinking about the environment; 2) Increase participants&#x27; interest and commitment to environmental issues; 3) Understand the importance of the ocean and its interrelationship with their lives and work.",
